Compile the programs using:

make

Or compile manually:

Baseline
g++ -O3 -fno-tree-vectorize main_baseline.cpp -o build/main_baseline

Auto-vectorized
g++ -O3 -march=native main_baseline.cpp -o build/main_autovec

AVX2
g++ -O3 -mavx2 -march=native main_avx.cpp -o build/main_avx

CUDA
nvcc -O3 main_cuda.cpp -o build/main_cuda

General usage:

./build/main_<version> N k seed warmup

Example:

./build/main_baseline 1000000 16 0 5
./build/main_autovec 1000000 16 0 5
./build/main_avx 1000000 16 0 5
./build/main_cuda 1000000 16 0 5

Parameters:

N = number of keys
k = number of partition bits (P = 2^k)
seed = random seed
warmup = number of warmup runs

Optional flags:

--json    save output to JSON file
--print   print mapping array (only for N<500)

Example:

./build/main_baseline 1000 16 0 5 --json --print

To run all experiments automatically:

python orchestrator.py

This script:

Runs baseline, auto-vectorized, AVX2, and CUDA versions
Checks correctness
Computes speedups
Computes Throughput

Saves results to:
results/results.json
Output

For each run, the following metrics are saved:

Execution time
Speedup
Checksum correctness
Array correctness (for N<500)